Package: sg-session
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         wine,
         cage,
         xwayland,
         x11-utils,
         procps,
         greetd,
         adduser
Description: Stained Glass OS session glue
 Brings up a Stained Glass desktop session: a compositor hosting Wine's
 explorer as the shell, running against a system-wide Wine prefix rather than
 a per-user one.
 .
 This package supplies the session entry point, the prefix initializer, the
 greetd integration and the scripted session check that the image boot gate
 consumes. It does not supply the compositor, the greeter or the shell itself;
 those are cage, greetd autologin and Wine's explorer during Phase 0.
